{"name":"Angelic Wings","hex":"#f4efee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angelic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging to, or proceeding from, angels; resembling, characteristic of, or partaking of the nature of, an angel.","Very sweet-natured, well-behaved, or beautiful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angelic"},{"term":"wings","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wing"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of scuba harness with an attached buoyancy compensation device: see wikipedia:Backplate and wing","A flip (hairstyle)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wings"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wing","blocks":[{"text":"A wing is a structure which produces both lift and drag while moving through air. Wings are defined by two shape characteristics, an airfoil section and a planform. Wing efficiency is expressed as lift-to-drag ratio, which compares the benefit of lift with the air resistance of a given wing shape, as it flies. Aerodynamics includes the study of wing performance in air."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg/330px-Wing.two.arp.600pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wing","wikidata":"Q161358"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG/500px-Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG/1280px-Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG/500px-Cloud_over_A340_wing.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Condensation in the low-pressure region over the wi